.TH LUS-TREE 1 "" "Lus" "Lus Manual"
.SH NAME
lus-tree \- print the modules a script requires, as a tree
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
\fBlus tree\fR [\-\-json] file
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Prints the modules that \fBfile\fR requires, and the modules they require, as a tree.
The tree follows the calls of \fBrequire\fR whose argument is a string literal.
It resolves each name against the templates of \fBLUS_PATH\fR, or of the default \fBpackage.path\fR when \fBLUS_PATH\fR is unset, relative to the current directory.
Each line names a module and the file it resolved to.
A module of the standard library, a remote module, and a name that resolves to no file end their branch.
A module that the tree already showed is marked \fB(*)\fR.
A file that also loads modules in a way the tree cannot follow, such as \fBrequire(name)\fR or \fBload\fR, is marked \fB(dynamic)\fR.
The exit status is 1 when a name resolves to no file or a file does not parse.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the tree as one JSON object per module with the fields \fBname\fR, \fBkind\fR, \fBpath\fR, \fBdynamic\fR, \fBrepeat\fR, and \fBrequires\fR.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
0
Every module resolved.
.TP
1
A name resolves to no file or a file does not parse.
.TP
2
An option is malformed or the file cannot be opened.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lus (1)
.PP
The CLI page of the Lus manual, https://lus.dev/manual/cli#lus-tree, has the same text with links to the rest of the manual.
